# Note-Taking Standard

Domain-agnostic rules for every create/update in this vault. Body quality bar and section names: follow `NOTES_STANDARD.md`. Navigation map: `INDEX.md`.

## Core principle

**Prefer UPDATE over CREATE.** One sharp note beats parallel stubs. Structure via `[[wikilinks]]` + light folders — do not invent deep taxonomy for each capture.

## Decision tree (run before writing)

1. **Durable knowledge?** No → skip or park briefly; do not create a permanent note for chores.
2. **Note already exists?** (search title / wikilink / folder) → **UPDATE that note.** Never duplicate.
3. **Else classify and CREATE:**
   - Named thing (tool, API, command, service, pattern instance) → **topic leaf**
   - Reusable idea/model (principle, framework, mental model) → **concept leaf**
   - New grouping that will hold many leaves → **area hub** (folder or hub note), then leaves
   - Comparison / symptom→note lookup / “X vs Y” → extend **`INDEX.md`** (or a Quick Reference), not a new genre
   - Vault/domain map → update **`INDEX.md`** / hub note

## Genres

| Genre | Role in this vault |
|-------|--------------------|
| Home / MOC | `INDEX.md`, domain hub notes |
| Quick Reference | Symptom tables in `INDEX.md`; cheat-sheet sections |
| Area hub | Topic folders + hub markdown that lists leaves |
| Topic leaf | One concrete subject (e.g. `ss`, `fsync`) |
| Concept leaf | Cross-cutting idea (e.g. `ACID`, mental models) |
| Inbox | Temporary only — process into a leaf, then clear |

## When UPDATING — where content goes

| Addition | Put it in |
|----------|-----------|
| One-line essence | Opening one-liner / quote |
| How it thinks | Mental model |
| Correct path | Standard config / commands |
| Breakage | Triage table (symptom → check → fix) |
| Silent failures | Gotchas |
| Anti-hammer | When NOT to use |
| Peers | Related `[[wikilinks]]` |

## When CREATING — checklist

1. Classify (topic / concept / area / INDEX edit)
2. Stable filename; prefer existing folder conventions over new top-level sprawl
3. Fill `NOTES_STANDARD.md` template (no empty headings, no wiki fluff)
4. Link Parent / Sibling / Related; add to area hub if one exists
5. Add retrieval row to `INDEX.md` when it helps under-pressure lookup
6. Merge duplicates instead of filling two thin notes

## Anti-patterns

- New note for every fleeting thought
- Parallel notes for the same subject
- Skipping INDEX/hub links after create
- Stuffing comparisons into deep leaves instead of INDEX
- Treating inbox captures as permanent graph nodes
- Empty stubs or command lists with no interpretation
